guys  with respect  i would like to just meet them in a dark  alley  i really would  um  and  i just think that you guys are such  incredible heroes so we wanted to say  thank you for everything that you do  i mean i'd love to hear your experience  thank you for listening to mine and my  mom's that left such an impression  on me  um but iman um like what were some of  the struggles that you went through any  stories to share um yeah so when the  pandemic started i was working at this  caribbean restaurant called tilly's and  when they shut down it's really  unfortunate it just moved in with my  partner  and so all of a sudden i had no income  and they really had to  you know take care of me and it really  put a strain on our relationship  especially because she was a registered  nurse going through the pandemic so  i wasn't working and she was working  overtime and thankfully when tilly's  opened back up they rehired me and it's  really just showing me about  adaptability and like rolling with the  punches you know  adaptability is something that i believe  in all my heart  is one of the most important character  traits that we can attain in this world  you can adapt that is a super power um  becky i was like i was wondering did you  have any social anxieties going back to  work like yay we're all together and yet  you're like oh it's so nice to see you  at six feet and a mask and washing my  hands  furiously like how was the psychology of  coming back as great as it was was there  any also like anxieties that came with  it yeah i think you know that's a normal  part to have some anxiety coming back  but once we were in the space um the  atmosphere that was built was just  people were excited you know we have  patrons who've been coming you know for  20 years and you know they know our  staff we had people even  who checked in on our staff every week  and um so it wasn't just you know like  this  throw you out there you know um to the  wolves people were welcoming people were  excited to be there and so that i think  eased  our anxieties and we were all being safe  you know we all made sure you know do  you feel comfortable you know socially  distancing sanitizing everything and  just  making sure that people have that i went  to a restaurant last night and the woman  would not let me in without my proof of  vaccination on my excelsior pass  my guarantee i'd keep my mask on and  then my driver's license to confirm  that um and i literally and she's like  look i'm sorry and i said  no  thank you for going these extra steps i  know not everybody wants to deal with  them and i'm sorry if anybody gives you  attitude because i'm very grateful for  you having to deal with each step that  this is taking you're amazing  um dana um you work at marie's crisis um  oh my god which is like  has anyone here been to marie's crisis  thank you and 10 gay men in the back um  it is all about singing and being packed  in together it is the most beautiful  energy and celebration of life  how is that functioning now what's your  experience been like how do you go from  sweating and singing and being packed in  together like sardines to the new normal  well at first when the pandemic and the  shutdown happened  our whole staff decided to get together  and go online  and sing and perform and stay connected  because we too have regulars who would  be there every day so we decided to make  a facebook group  they were amazing they supported us  and we went from 200 followers to 20 000  overnight wow  um i just want to thank you for sharing  your incredible stories with us and um  we want to get you guys dinner on all of  us um so we're going to give you a 200  gift card to some of the best  restaurants in new york which you're  already you know working in and and  frequenting and our friends at the  american licorice company red vines they  want to tip you guys a thousand dollars  each  so  thank you  thank you  thank you red vine  [Applause]  thank you  thank you  there's just something so much better  about cash you know it's just so much  more instant gratification i just thank  you so much for being such wonderful  people and keep going out there and  letting us know how we can serve you  [Music]

